# Per-user, per-machine paths. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and edit:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `src/__init__.py` loads `.env` on the first `src.` import, so it reaches `run_project.py`, every stage subprocess,
# `pytest` and `scripts/*` without anything being exported by hand.
#
# ⚠️ AN ALREADY-SET VARIABLE ALWAYS WINS. An explicit `export`, and the environment slurm hands a job, both override
# this file — so a launch script that sets its own paths keeps working, and `.env` is the fallback rather than the
# authority. Nothing here is secret; it is paths only.
#
# Syntax: `KEY=VALUE`, one per line. `#` starts a comment (whole-line, or after whitespace at the end of a value).
# Quote a value to keep it verbatim. A line that is not an assignment RAISES rather than being skipped, because a
# typo that silently sets nothing is the failure this file exists to remove.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The read-only dataset: metadata.json, metadata.csv, samples/, scalers/. Interpolated into config as
# `{{$DATA_ROOT}}` (11 places). Missing, it fails inside `prepare_modeling` rather than at parse time.
DATA_ROOT=/path/to/era5_postprocess

# Everything the pipelines WRITE: prepared/, tuning/, best/, evaluation/, reports/. Interpolated as
# `{{$OUTPUT_ROOT}}` (261 places). Keep it off the source filesystem — one daily prepared directory is ~20 GiB
# (features/ alone is 19.7 GiB per split) and the three families come to ~60 GiB.
#
# Missing, `setup` refuses the run and names the variable: `{{$VAR}}` substitutes to the EMPTY STRING, so
# '{{$OUTPUT_ROOT}}/family/prepared' becomes '/family/prepared' — absolute, at the filesystem root.
OUTPUT_ROOT=/scratch/your-user/lightning-outputs

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where MLflow keeps run metadata and logged artifacts. UNSET means the checkout: `./mlruns/` for artifacts, and the
# run metadata wherever the default backend puts it. Point it out of the tree to keep the clone clean.
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=file:/scratch/your-user/lightning-outputs/mlruns

# The upstream checkpoint the two stochastic families build on. Deliberately commented out: it is a per-RUN path, not
# per-machine config, and UNSET is meaningful — it means "no warm start", which is how each family runs standalone.
# ⚠️ The two families read it at different stages and want different things: mc_dropout wants the upstream's WEIGHTS
# (read by `tune`), diffusion wants its PREDICTIONS (materialised by `prepare_modeling`).
# UPSTREAM_MODEL=/scratch/your-user/lightning-outputs/deterministic_unet/best/best_model.ckpt

# Natural Earth data for cartopy. UNSET is correct: the bootstrap points this at the coastline committed under
# `data/cartopy` when that directory exists, so plotting needs no network. Set it only to override that.
# CARTOPY_DATA_DIR=/path/to/cartopy

# ⛔ DO NOT set PIPELINE_SEED here. The orchestrator derives it per stage from that stage's code state and parameters
# and exports it before dispatching the subprocess; a value in this file would be overridden anyway, and reading one
# here would suggest the seed is a user setting when it is a derived one.
